sm8750-common: sensors: integrate AlsCorrection to SensorsSubHal

1. The namespace has been adjusted to match our SensorsSubHal.
2. Not all devices on sm8750 use a wrapped wise_rgb sensor. For exmaple,
   dodge has a normal android.sensor.light sensor which reports a single
   scalar value as the measured lux. Therefore, AlsCorrection should be
   able to correctly pick either the data[2] of wise_rgb or the scalar
   of android.sensor.light. A new parameter "is_wise_rgb" is added to
   the process() function to make the selection.
3. The postEvents() in SensorsSubHal has been reworked to always make a
   copy of the incoming event vector. The interface passes a const
   reference of the vector, so the SensorsSubHal cannot directly modify
   one of the event. When compensating the scalar value of
   android.sensor.light, technically it is possible to only make a copy
   of the event itself, compensate the value, and then append it to the
   callback vector. The problem is that the old uncompensated event also
   needs to be removed from the vector, which is non-trivial. In the
   end, it is simpler to copy the whole vector for processing.

Signed-off-by: Chenyang Zhong <zhongcy95@gmail.com>

